# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
# The dashboard is a client-side-routed SPA (see src/lib/routes.ts): /review,
# /files, /docs, etc. are rendered in the browser, not as separate HTML files.
# Without this rule a hard load of a deep link (or a refresh on /review) 404s.
# Mirror of the Netlify `[[redirects]] /* -> /index.html 200` in netlify.toml.
#
# Files that exist are served as themselves, before this rewrite (live
# 2026-09-24: /data/factstack.json → application/json, /robots.txt →
# text/plain), so /mcp-auth-config.json needs no exclusion here. If it comes
# back as text/html, that deploy was built WITHOUT it and this rule served
# index.html — `gen-fb-config.mjs --require` in deploy:cf now blocks that.
#
# NOTE: do NOT add a 404.html + a `/assets/* /404.html 404` rule. On Cloudflare
# Pages a 404.html in the build output takes precedence over this 200 catch-all
# and breaks the SPA fallback (deep links like /files start returning 404). A
# missing hashed asset falling through to index.html (200) is the accepted
# SPA-on-CF trade-off — it's near-impossible anyway with immutable hashed
# assets + atomic deploys. (Verified live 2026-06-15: the 404.html approach
# 404'd every client route.)
/*  /index.html  200
